# API Information


main: {
  kit: {
    info: {
      contact: {
        email: "[email protected]"
      }
      description: "This API allows users to generate QR codes based on specified data and size. You can customize the output by providing the data to encode and the desired dimensions in pixels."
      servers: [
        {
          description: "Production server"
          url: "https://api.apgy.in"
        }
      ]
      title: "QR Code Generator"
      version: "1.0.0"
      tagline: "Generate QR codes from arbitrary data at a configurable pixel size via a single HTTP GET"
      homepage: "https://api.apgy.in"
      docs_url: "https://freepublicapis.com/qr-code-generator"
      about_md: `The QR Code Generator API is a small public service hosted at [api.apgy.in](https://api.apgy.in) that turns arbitrary input data into a QR code image. It is catalogued on [Free Public APIs](https://freepublicapis.com/qr-code-generator) alongside other lightweight, no-key utility APIs.

What you get from the API:

- A single \`GET /qr/\` endpoint that returns a QR code rendered from the supplied \`data\` value
- A configurable output \`size\` so callers can request the pixel dimensions they need

Operational notes: the upstream service has been flagged as intermittently unreachable on community trackers, so callers should expect to handle network errors and consider caching generated codes. No authentication, licence, or rate-limit information is published.`
      entity_desc: {
        qrn: "Represents a generated QR code image produced from the supplied data and size, served by the `GET /qr/` endpoint."
      }
      auth: false
    }
  }
}
